928
00:38:55.150 --> 00:39:00.710
I did discuss Brenda in fast facts, but we were going to come to you and ask you for your input about Brenda.
我在快问快答里确实讨论过布伦达，但我们本来打算找你来谈谈你对布伦达的看法。

929
00:39:00.950 --> 00:39:05.970
Well, Brenda was Mindy's writing and performance partner in the play.
嗯，布伦达是明迪在话剧里的编剧兼搭档。

930
00:39:05.970 --> 00:39:16.050
That is how I cast Mindy, because Mindy wrote this off-Broadway play called Matt and Ben about Matt Damon and Ben Affleck writing Good Will Hunting.
这就是我选中明迪的原因，因为明迪写了一部外百老汇话剧叫《马特与本》，讲的是马特·达蒙和本·阿弗莱克写《心灵捕手》的故事。

931
00:39:16.050 --> 00:39:24.430
And Mindy played Ben Affleck and Brenda, who's in Booze Cruise, played Matt Damon.
明迪饰演本·阿弗莱克，而参演《乘船狂欢》的布伦达则饰演马特·达蒙。

932
00:39:24.630 --> 00:39:26.250
And it was a hilarious play.
那真是一部 hilarious 的话剧。

933
00:39:26.450 --> 00:39:27.350
You went and saw it?
你去看过了？

934
00:39:27.390 --> 00:39:28.070
Yes, I went and saw it.
对，我去看过了。

935
00:39:28.070 --> 00:39:29.610
By accident or on purpose?
是偶然去的还是特意去的？

936
00:39:29.830 --> 00:39:38.230
No, I was actually, I was a guest of my wife, Suzanne Daniels, who was a network executive, possibly at the WB at that time.
不，其实我是作为我妻子苏珊·丹尼尔斯的嘉宾去的，她当时是一位电视网高管，可能当时在WB工作吧。

937
00:39:38.250 --> 00:39:39.770
I'm not exactly sure where she was working.
我不太确定她当时在哪里工作。

938
00:39:39.770 --> 00:39:47.630
And she went to see it to do talent scouting, and I thought it was super funny, yeah.
她去看是为了物色人才，我觉得超级搞笑，真的。

939
00:39:47.890 --> 00:39:49.090
And it was great.
而且棒极了。

940
00:39:49.270 --> 00:39:57.630
And then, by coincidence, Mindy's spec script came in, like, the next day for me to read for staffing for writers.
然后，很巧的是，明迪的样片剧本就在第二天送到了我手里，让我为编剧团队进行评估。

941
00:39:57.730 --> 00:39:59.450
And I was like, hey, wait, that's the one I just saw.
当时我就想，嘿，等等，这不就是我刚刚看过的那部吗。

942
00:40:00.510 --> 00:40:00.990
Amazing.
太神奇了。

943
00:40:01.310 --> 00:40:01.360
Yeah.
对啊。

944
00:40:01.810 --> 00:40:02.210
Amazing.
太神奇了。

945
00:40:02.450 --> 00:40:02.730
Terrific.
太棒了。

946
00:40:03.150 --> 00:40:03.490
Wow.
哇。

947
00:40:03.490 --> 00:40:04.650
I would have loved to have seen that.
我当时要是能看一眼就好了。

948
00:40:04.810 --> 00:40:08.430
So now we have Brenda, and she's, like, the corporate person.
所以现在我们有了布伦达，她就像是那种公司职员。

949
00:40:08.430 --> 00:40:10.790
You guys, I just have to point out something about Brenda.
伙计们，我必须指出关于布伦达的一点。

950
00:40:11.050 --> 00:40:15.030
I know we're not on the boat yet, but Brenda drinks the whole boat ride.
我知道我们还没上船，但布伦达在整段船程里都在喝酒。

951
00:40:16.070 --> 00:40:17.970
She's there to check in on Michael.
她去那里是为了看看迈克尔的情况。

952
00:40:18.170 --> 00:40:19.550
She has a beer in her hand.
她手里拿着一杯啤酒。

953
00:40:19.690 --> 00:40:20.110
You look.
你看。

954
00:40:20.230 --> 00:40:21.690
Look at her scenes on the boat.
看看她在船上的那些戏份。

955
00:40:21.850 --> 00:40:23.450
She has a beer the whole time.
她全程都拿着一杯啤酒。

956
00:40:23.590 --> 00:40:24.350
She's at the bar.
她在酒吧里。

957
00:40:24.510 --> 00:40:26.710
I mean, he only sees her when she's at the bar, pretty much.
我的意思是，基本上他只有在她去酒吧时才能见到她。

958
00:40:26.770 --> 00:40:27.290
Pretty much.
基本上是这样。

959
00:40:27.410 --> 00:40:30.670
Or she walks up with a beer, like, to check in on him.
或者她拿着啤酒走过来，就好像是去查看他的情况。

960
00:40:31.050 --> 00:40:34.490
Wait, before we get out of the conference room scene, Phyllis broke so hard.
等等，在我们离开会议室那场戏之前，菲利斯笑场得太厉害了。

961
00:40:34.490 --> 00:40:35.550
Do you remember this?
你还记得这个吗？

962
00:40:36.150 --> 00:40:36.810
Oh, yes.
哦，记得。

963
00:40:36.810 --> 00:40:37.570
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

964
00:40:37.570 --> 00:40:42.790
So Michael has said that the sales team could be, is, like, the furnace of the ship.
所以迈克尔曾说过销售团队可能是，就是，像这艘船的锅炉房。

965
00:40:43.450 --> 00:40:45.550
Because it keeps things moving along.
因为这让事情得以顺利推进。

966
00:40:45.550 --> 00:40:45.870
Yes.
是的。

967
00:40:46.070 --> 00:40:49.770
He compares them to the people from Titanic.
他把他们比作《泰坦尼克号》里的人。

968
00:40:50.090 --> 00:40:50.450
Right.
没错。

969
00:40:50.630 --> 00:40:51.070
Titanic.
泰坦尼克号。

970
00:40:51.370 --> 00:40:55.830
And at 5 minutes, 20 seconds, Phyllis has to put her head down because she starts laughing
而在5分20秒的时候，菲利斯不得不低下头，因为她开始笑了

971
00:40:55.830 --> 00:40:59.030
because she says, she asks what the furnace does.
因为她说，她问锅炉房是做什么用的。

972
00:40:59.030 --> 00:41:03.490
And then at 5 minutes, 50 seconds, she says, everyone in the engine room drown.
然后在5分50秒时，她说，机舱里的所有人都淹死了。

973
00:41:03.950 --> 00:41:04.630
Do you remember that?
你还记得那个吗？

974
00:41:04.650 --> 00:41:04.930
Yes.
记得。

975
00:41:04.930 --> 00:41:06.930
She could not get out the word drown.
她怎么也说不出“淹死”这个词。

976
00:41:07.230 --> 00:41:08.070
Like, she couldn't.
就是说，她说不出口。

977
00:41:08.150 --> 00:41:09.430
She just broke every time.
她每次都忍不住笑场。

978
00:41:09.430 --> 00:41:11.990
And you can see her, like, starting to break.
你可以看到她，好像开始憋不住了。

979
00:41:12.230 --> 00:41:14.450
That made me break on the day.
那在拍摄当天也让我笑场了。

980
00:41:14.550 --> 00:41:15.390
Yes, me too.
是的，我也是。

981
00:41:15.390 --> 00:41:19.370
Phyllis so sadly realized that everyone in the engine room drowned.
菲利斯无比悲伤地意识到机舱里的所有人都淹死了。

982
00:41:19.710 --> 00:41:21.170
She's like, but Michael, everyone drowned.
她就好像在说，可是迈克尔，大家都淹死了。

983
00:41:21.590 --> 00:41:25.730
Well, now let's, we have to have the moment everyone gets on the boat.
好了，现在我们得，我们得说说大家都上船的那个时刻。

984
00:41:25.890 --> 00:41:27.270
We've left the conference room.
我们已经离开会议室了。

985
00:41:27.410 --> 00:41:27.730
Yes.
是的。

986
00:41:27.870 --> 00:41:28.890
We're jumping around a little.
我们跳跃着剪辑了一点。

987
00:41:29.350 --> 00:41:34.170
At 6 minutes, 20 seconds, Michael says that Pam is Mary Ann.
在6分20秒时，迈克尔说帕姆是玛丽·安。

988
00:41:34.170 --> 00:41:36.750
Katie and Jim are the Professor and Ginger.
凯蒂和吉姆是教授和金杰。

989
00:41:37.330 --> 00:41:38.490
Angela's Mrs. Howell.
安吉拉是豪威尔夫人。

990
00:41:39.010 --> 00:41:39.810
Kelly's the native.
凯莉是土著。

991
00:41:40.610 --> 00:41:42.170
Stanley is one of the Globetrotters.
斯坦利是哈林环球旅行者队的队员之一。

992
00:41:42.410 --> 00:41:43.270
Michael is the Skipper.
迈克尔是船长。

993
00:41:43.410 --> 00:41:44.370
And Dwight is Gilligan.
而德怀特是吉利根。

994
00:41:44.530 --> 00:41:48.830
And this begins the war between Captain Jack and Captain Michael.
这就拉开了杰克船长和迈克尔船长之间战争的序幕。

995
00:41:49.130 --> 00:41:49.590
Yes.
是的。

996
00:41:49.730 --> 00:41:54.850
I love that Michael has worn his Captain hat to the booze cruise.
我喜欢迈克尔戴着他的船长帽去游船派对。

997
00:41:55.290 --> 00:41:57.890
He has it on in the booze cruise and he still has it on.
他在游船派对上戴着它，现在还戴着。

998
00:41:57.890 --> 00:42:00.290
And now they're having their little power struggle.
现在他们正在进行权力争夺。

999
00:42:00.610 --> 00:42:03.330
Who is going to be the boss of this trip?
谁将成为这次旅行的老板？

1000
00:42:04.130 --> 00:42:06.250
Captain Jack is clearly going to win.
杰克船长显然会赢。

1001
00:42:06.510 --> 00:42:09.870
I mean, I feel like his boundary is very strong from the beginning.
我的意思是，我觉得他从一开始的界限感就很强。

1002
00:42:10.030 --> 00:42:10.550
Very strong.
非常强。

1003
00:42:10.710 --> 00:42:11.410
And I want you to know.
我想让你知道。

1004
00:42:11.410 --> 00:42:13.450
We should say Captain Jack played by Rob Riggle.
我们得说一下由罗布·里格尔饰演的杰克船长。

1005
00:42:13.630 --> 00:42:13.910
Yes.
没错。

1006
00:42:14.170 --> 00:42:14.850
Who was a Marine.
他曾是一名海军陆战队员。

1007
00:42:15.070 --> 00:42:15.290
Yes.
对。

1008
00:42:15.290 --> 00:42:15.830
Who was a Marine.
他曾是一名海军陆战队员。

1009
00:42:15.970 --> 00:42:16.190
Yes.
是的。

1010
00:42:16.390 --> 00:42:16.550
Yes.
没错。

1011
00:42:16.550 --> 00:42:21.110
So there's a lot of authenticity to Captain Jack's military bearing there.
所以杰克船长的军人仪态非常有真实感。

1012
00:42:21.290 --> 00:42:22.250
How did you find Rob?
你们是怎么找到罗布的？

1013
00:42:22.810 --> 00:42:24.750
Well, I mean, you know Rob, right?
嗯，我的意思是，你认识罗布，对吧？

1014
00:42:24.790 --> 00:42:25.450
I know Rob.
我认识罗布。

1015
00:42:25.450 --> 00:42:29.730
We talked a little bit about it in one of our Fast Facts, but Rob wanted me to give
我们在其中一期“快速问答”里稍微聊过，但罗布让我给你

1016
00:42:29.730 --> 00:42:30.590
you a message.
捎个信。

1017
00:42:30.710 --> 00:42:30.890
Yeah.
是吗。

1018
00:42:30.970 --> 00:42:33.910
Because I talked to him yesterday and he said, thank you so much.
因为我昨天跟他聊过，他说非常感谢。

1019
00:42:34.310 --> 00:42:36.990
Also, he's sorry that he couldn't say Lake Wall and Pawpuck.
另外，他很遗憾没能念对“拉克沃尔”和“鲍帕克”。

1020
00:42:39.170 --> 00:42:41.870
Rob was, you know, in the Allison Jones orbit.
罗布以前在埃利森·琼斯的圈子里。

1021
00:42:42.250 --> 00:42:42.390
Yeah.
对。

1022
00:42:42.410 --> 00:42:45.150
So, and we certainly knew about him.
所以，我们当然知道他。

1023
00:42:45.950 --> 00:42:49.670
And I don't know whether he came in for one of the other parts.
我记不清他是不是来试过其他角色。

1024
00:42:49.810 --> 00:42:51.590
Like he might have come in for Dwight or something.
比如他可能来试过德怀特什么的。

1025
00:42:51.730 --> 00:42:52.750
I'm not 100% sure.
我不敢百分之百确定。

1026
00:42:53.050 --> 00:42:54.010
Did that happen sometimes?
这种情况有时会发生吗？

1027
00:42:54.010 --> 00:42:57.270
And sometimes people who had come in for main cast members, you would ping them for
而且有时候对于来试过主要演员的人，你们会把他们记下来留作

1028
00:42:57.270 --> 00:42:58.230
a future episode.
以后某集的备选。

1029
00:42:58.470 --> 00:42:58.710
Sure.
当然。

1030
00:42:58.970 --> 00:42:59.150
Yeah.
对。

1031
00:42:59.150 --> 00:43:05.990
I mean, I think Allison released some of the audition tapes as part of a DVD extra, but
我的意思是，我觉得埃利森作为DVD花絮公开了一些试镜带，但

1032
00:43:05.990 --> 00:43:08.070
there were a lot of cool people that came in.
当时来了很多很棒的人。

1033
00:43:08.130 --> 00:43:10.630
It would have been very interesting to see Seth Rogen as Dwight, for instance.
比如说，能看到塞斯·罗根演德怀特一定会非常有趣。

1034
00:43:10.910 --> 00:43:11.190
Yes.
对的。

1035
00:43:11.370 --> 00:43:11.690
Definitely.
绝对的。

1036
00:43:12.350 --> 00:43:13.870
Or Kristen Wiig as Pam.
或者克里斯汀·韦格演帕姆。

1037
00:43:14.050 --> 00:43:14.170
Yeah.
对。

1038
00:43:14.170 --> 00:43:15.590
I think she came in to read Pam.
我觉得她当时是来试读帕姆的。

1039
00:43:15.870 --> 00:43:16.010
Yeah.
对。

1040
00:43:16.010 --> 00:43:19.070
I think she's in my sign, on my, on my, on my, Allison Jones.
我觉得她在我那份、我的、我的、埃利森·琼斯的签到表上。

1041
00:43:19.110 --> 00:43:19.490
And Catherine Hahn.
还有凯瑟琳·哈恩。

1042
00:43:19.670 --> 00:43:19.870
Yeah.
对。

1043
00:43:20.310 --> 00:43:26.310
Allison Jones gave me my sign in sheet day and Catherine Hahn is on it and Bob Odenkirk
埃利森·琼斯给了我当天的签到表，凯瑟琳·哈恩在上面，鲍勃·奥登科克

1044
00:43:26.310 --> 00:43:26.810
is on it.
也在上面。

1045
00:43:26.890 --> 00:43:27.030
Yeah.
对。

1046
00:43:27.250 --> 00:43:29.750
Well, Bob was really the number two.
嗯，鲍勃真的是第二人选。

1047
00:43:29.890 --> 00:43:32.190
If we, if we didn't have Steve, it would have been Bob.
如果我们、如果我们没有史蒂夫，那就会是鲍勃。

1048
00:43:32.350 --> 00:43:33.050
He did a great job.
他表现得棒极了。

1049
00:43:33.210 --> 00:43:36.190
And then in season nine, we brought him back as the sort of echo.
然后在第九季，我们让他回来客串了一个类似翻版的角色。

1050
00:43:36.410 --> 00:43:38.250
He was so fantastic too.
他也表现得太棒了。

1051
00:43:38.430 --> 00:43:38.570
Yeah.
是啊。

1052
00:43:39.470 --> 00:43:40.090
He's great.
他很棒。

1053
00:43:40.090 --> 00:43:43.130
So I have a lot of fan questions about the boat.
所以我有许多粉丝关于这艘船的问题。

1054
00:43:43.330 --> 00:43:43.590
Sure.
当然。

1055
00:43:43.770 --> 00:43:44.010
Okay.
好的。

1056
00:43:44.430 --> 00:43:49.690
So since we're getting on the boat, Casey Wright asked, was the boat really moving?
既然我们要上船了，凯西·赖特（Casey Wright）问，船真的在动吗？

1057
00:43:49.950 --> 00:43:52.570
And Sam Pellett asked how cold it was.
萨姆·佩利特（Sam Pellett）问当时有多冷。

1058
00:43:52.750 --> 00:43:56.050
The boat was really moving through the water for one of the days of shooting.
在拍摄的其中一天，船确实在水面上行驶。

1059
00:43:56.170 --> 00:43:59.470
The other two days, I believe it was docked and it was cold.
另外两天，我相信它是停靠着的，而且很冷。

1060
00:43:59.470 --> 00:44:04.590
It was December, 2005, which was chilly, especially at night out on the water.
那是2005年12月，天气很寒冷，尤其是夜晚在水面上。

1061
00:44:04.810 --> 00:44:08.370
A lot of people wondered, were you pretending to be that cold?
很多人想知道，你们是在假装那么冷吗？

1062
00:44:08.370 --> 00:44:10.410
I remember being cold.
我记得当时真的很冷。

1063
00:44:10.710 --> 00:44:10.770
I don't think, yeah, yes.
我觉得，是的，没错。

1064
00:44:11.150 --> 00:44:12.670
I don't think there was a lot of pretending.
我觉得用不着怎么假装。

1065
00:44:12.670 --> 00:44:15.330
Your cheeks are like bright pink in that scene.
你在那一幕里双颊粉红。

1066
00:44:15.510 --> 00:44:15.870
Yes.
是的。

1067
00:44:16.210 --> 00:44:22.870
So Lorne Michaels has a thing that he says sometimes where like he will get in character
所以洛恩·迈克尔斯（Lorne Michaels）有时会说一句话，就好像他会为演员准备符合角色的

1068
00:44:22.870 --> 00:44:24.650
underwear for the actors.
内衣。

1069
00:44:25.170 --> 00:44:25.430
Oh.
哦。

1070
00:44:26.270 --> 00:44:27.890
And yeah, I think this is it.
对，我想就是这样。

1071
00:44:28.590 --> 00:44:29.990
And people will say, well, why?
人们会说，好吧，为什么呢？

1072
00:44:30.110 --> 00:44:30.570
Who cares?
谁在乎呢？

1073
00:44:30.690 --> 00:44:31.770
It's not going to be on camera.
反正镜头又拍不到。

1074
00:44:31.850 --> 00:44:33.030
And he goes, yes, but the actors know.
而他说，是的，但演员自己知道。

1075
00:44:34.030 --> 00:44:35.290
I kind of get that.
我有点理解这个。

1076
00:44:35.350 --> 00:44:35.510
Yeah.
是啊。

1077
00:44:35.830 --> 00:44:36.910
I kind of get that.
我有点理解。

1078
00:44:36.910 --> 00:44:41.790
And so we certainly believed in that and went out on this real boat in Long Beach Harbor
所以我们确实坚信这一点，去了长滩港的一艘真正的船上，

1079
00:44:41.790 --> 00:44:42.890
and it was this huge thing.
那是一件大事。

1080
00:44:43.170 --> 00:44:52.830
And to me, the key of it was that romantic scene on the top deck between Pam and Jim.
对我来说，其中的关键是帕姆和吉姆在顶层甲板上的那场浪漫戏。

1081
00:44:54.950 --> 00:44:59.590
And I just thought it'd be so pretty up there with the twinkling lights of the harbor in
我只是觉得上面会很美，背景是港口闪烁的灯光

1082
00:44:59.590 --> 00:45:00.430
the background and everything.
以及一切景色。

1083
00:45:00.430 --> 00:45:08.190
